                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 4,
                "retweet_count": 6,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I'll save you all the trouble of reading this weird, meandering, lie-filled rant by Trump.\n\nEssentially, he wants to shut down the down the government because he's afraid to negotiate with Democrats who want to ensure your healthcare costs DON'T go up.\n\nGovernment funding runs out on September 30. At the same time, the American people are facing a Republican health care crisis that is driving up costs.\n\nThe Republican spending bill has already failed in the Senate and didn't even get all the Republicans to vote for it. To keep government open and lower costs, we need bipartisan negotiations right now. \n\nInstead, Republican's have skipped town, Trump has canceled his meetings, and Speaker Johnson has canceled our voting days next week before the shutdown. \n\nIf the government shuts down, Trump and Republicans will have no one to blame but themselves.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1758651669,
                "view_count": 3388
